// PARKED REPRO (silent miscompile -- an UNDECLARED bare name is accepted). `let x
// = undeclared_var` where `undeclared_var` is not a local, parameter, or field
// COMPILES at --check AND --build-dir and RUNS (exit 0 -- the undeclared name reads
// as 0/garbage). No error at any phase. A bare name is resolved for value but never
// checked for EXISTENCE. (The `self.<field>` typo case IS caught -- see
// unknown_field_read_rejected -- but a bare single-segment name is not.)
//
// A related opaque case: `exit_process(undeclared_var)` errors, but with a
// misleading "host operation has no encodable call sequence" from the BACKEND
// encoder, not "unknown name" from the checker.
//
// VALID bare-name set (probed 2026-07-04): a single-segment bare name resolves to a
// LOCAL (`let`), a PARAMETER, or a FIELD (implicit `self`, e.g. bare `fld` == `self.fld`).
// All three verified accepted; a nonexistent bare name verified silently accepted.
//
// FIX SKETCH -- ATTEMPTED + REVERTED 2026-07-04 (18 whole-tail false positives).
// The naive "1-segment Name not in {field, local, param, top-level symbol, enum
// case}" check in scan_expression_calls IS NOT SUFFICIENT. The allow-list built
// from machine_symbols.has_member/has_owned_data/contained_type + symbols.has_type/
// machine/platform/trait_definition + state params + state LocalData + data-variant
// cases correctly accepted a bare field/local/enum-case in isolation, but the whole
// corpus surfaced TWO more legal forms it wrongly rejected:
//   1. `true` / `false` are represented as single-segment `Name` nodes here (NOT
//      Boolean-literal nodes) in some lowerings -- so a bare boolean tripped the
//      check. Must special-case `true`/`false` (or, better, detect boolean-literal
//      names earlier).
//   2. CROSS-STATE SCOPE: a SUB-state reads a param/local of the machine's ENTRY (or
//      an ancestor) state -- e.g. `state nonpos` reads `n`, `state mark_current_room`
//      reads `room_index` -- which are declared on a DIFFERENT state. Looking up only
//      `program.state_parameters(<current state>)` + the current state's LocalData
//      MISSES these. The real scope is the machine's threaded binding environment
//      across states, not one state's params/locals.
// So the check needs the actual NAME-RESOLUTION SCOPE (threaded params/locals across
// a machine's states + boolean-literal names), i.e. real name resolution -- a
// focused-session feature, NOT the local-lookup sketch. Symbol API located (for the
// eventual work): MachineSymbols::{has_member,has_owned_data,contained_type};
// TopLevelSymbols::{has_type,machine,platform,trait_definition}; cases via
// program.data_members -> DataMember::Variant. Bare enum cases ARE legal
// (`let s: Signal = Red` compiles). MEASURE the whole tail (18 fp last time).

boundary trait Console { machine exit_process(return_code: i32); }

data Main { console: Console; }

machine Main::main(&mut self) {
    let x: i32 in Wrapping = undeclared_var; // undeclared bare name -- silently accepted, reads 0
    self.console.exit_process(x);
}
